      "name": "ELK-BLEDOM Service",
      "notes": "Single service with one write characteristic. Write-only — the device sends no responses. All packets use the 9-byte format: [0x7E] [seq] [cmd] [p1] [p2] [p3] [p4] [flag] [0xEF].\nByte 2 (sequence) can be 0x00 for basic operation. Byte 8 (flag) is typically 0x00 or 0x10 — both work identically.\n",
